{"ref":"BDB, בֹּ֫עַז","hw":"בֹּ֫עַז","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בֹּ֫עַז</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. (</strong><em>quickness</em>?<strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>1.</strong>  kinsman of Naomi, who married Ruth <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:1\" href=\"/Ruth.2.1\">Ru 2:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:3\" href=\"/Ruth.2.3\">3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:4\" href=\"/Ruth.2.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:5\" href=\"/Ruth.2.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:8\" href=\"/Ruth.2.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:11\" href=\"/Ruth.2.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:14\" href=\"/Ruth.2.14\">14</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:15\" href=\"/Ruth.2.15\">15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:19\" href=\"/Ruth.2.19\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:23\" href=\"/Ruth.2.23\">23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ruth 3:2\" href=\"/Ruth.3.2\">3:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 3:7\" href=\"/Ruth.3.7\">7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:1\" href=\"/Ruth.4.1\">4:1</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:5\" href=\"/Ruth.4.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:8\" href=\"/Ruth.4.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:9\" href=\"/Ruth.4.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:13\" href=\"/Ruth.4.13\">13</a>, also v <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:21\" href=\"/Ruth.4.21\">21</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:11\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.11\">1 Ch 2:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:12\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.12\">12</a> (𝔊 Βοος, Βοοζ).<br><strong>2.</strong>  name of the left hand of two pillars set up before temple (cf. also <a data-ref=\"BDB, יָכִין\" href=\"/BDB,_יָכִין\", dir=\"rtl\">יָכִין</a> sub <a data-ref=\"BDB, יָכִין\" href=\"/BDB,_יָכִין\", dir=\"rtl\">כון</a>) <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:21\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.21\">1 K 7:21</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 3:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.3.17\">2 Ch 3:17</a>; <strong>(</strong>meaning obscure; MT appar. ref. to <strong>1</strong>, cf. 𝔗 <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 3:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.3.17\">2 Ch 3:17</a>; Thes supposes name of architect or donor; Ew perhaps sons of Solomon, etc.; read possibly <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּעֹז</span> <em>in strength</em>, 𝔊 <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 3:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.3.17\">2 Ch 3:17</a> ἰσχύς; Th thinks <span dir=\"rtl\">יכין בעז</span> a sentence, one word being engraved on each pillar, <em>he</em> (God) <em>established in strength;</em> against him, however, Ke Be; Öt thinks an exclamation, <em>in strength!</em> expressing satisfaction of architect; Klo proposes for <span dir=\"rtl\">בעז</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּעַל עֹז</span> (cf. B <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:21\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.21\">1 K 7:21</a> Βαλαζ)<strong>)</strong>.","next":"BDB, בָּעַט","prev":"BDB, בעז"}